  "result": "Perfect! All 407 tests pass. The `mergeCustomers` function is now complete.\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n**Added `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` to src/customers.js:**\n\n- **Returns** `ok({ customers, invoices })` where the `fromId` customer is removed and all their invoices are reassigned to `intoId`\n- **Errors:**\n  - `SAME_CUSTOMER` if attempting to merge a customer into itself\n  - `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if either customer ID doesn't exist\n- **Features:**\n  - Normalizes both IDs (trim whitespace, convert to uppercase)\n  - Preserves all invoice fields except `customerId`\n  - Removes `fromId` customer from the customers array\n  - Leaves unrelated customers and invoices unchanged\n\n**Added 13 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Basic merge and customer removal\n- Both error cases with proper validation\n- ID normalization (lowercase, spaces, mixed case)\n- Multiple invoices being updated correctly\n- Preservation of invoice data and unrelated customers\n- Edge cases (empty invoices, no matching invoices)\n\nAll tests pass: **407/407** \u2713",
